  "$comment": "Tesco (tesco.com) tracking config fragments — reference copy only, loaded by nothing. To use, paste the arrays into a study config under tracking.* (contract: docs/config-schema.md §3.1/§3.2; guides: docs/README.md → 'Semantic-group (sg) rules' and 'Force-tracked elements'). Tesco's 2026 DDS-web (CSS-modules) build renders product tiles with two different components, so there is one sg rule per markup variant — the variants' selectors are disjoint, so whichever isn't present on a page is inert. (1) Carousel / recommendation tile (homepage, 'you may also like' rails): <section data-testid='product-<id>' data-product-id='<id>' aria-label='<product name>'> — the tile stamps the clean name on its own aria-label (first source), the h2 title link text is the fallback, and the tile's data-testid (product_<id>) is the last resort. The tile also holds a nested attribute-less <section> around promotions + buybox; closest() walks past it to the outer tile. (2) Listing / search grid tile (groceries, browse, search — ul[data-testid='dynamic-grid'] > li): <li data-testid='<id>'> with no data-product-id or aria-label, so the container is identified by the product-tile heading it contains (:has) and named from that heading's link text, then any h2 product link, then the bare numeric data-testid. Anchor only on data-* attributes, the design-system's public ddsweb-* classes and the semantic online-components-product-tile-* BEM classes — the _1bCRSG_* / rWr0Xq_* / Y4g-HG_* / WL_DZkV_* tokens are CSS-module hashes and the carousel ids (ddsweb-ghs-carousel-_r_2_) are React-generated; all change across builds/renders. additionalTrackedElements force-tracks the fragments the heuristics roll up into the tile text, again per variant: carousel tile — buybox price <p>s (price_retail = first <p> of the price container, e.g. £64.99; price_unit = a second <p>, not present on the marketplace sample this was derived from, kept as an inert guess), promotion value bar (price_promo = 'Was £89.99 Now £64.99' / Clubcard-price style text; promo_terms = 'Offer valid until …'), delivery line (delivery_message = 'Sold by Marketplace seller.'); grid tile — price text (price_retail = £13.79), unit price (price_unit = £22.98/kg), fulfilment line (delivery_message = '£2.99 Courier Delivery by Mon 19 Oct. Sold by Marketplace seller.'). The offer-sash badge (badge = 'Marketplace.' and other tags) uses the same ddsweb-tag class in both variants. Quantity controls (shown once a product is in the trolley) come in two markups too, so there is one trio of entries per variant: the carousel tile uses the design-system component (ddsweb-quantity-controls-* data-auto buttons, count in .ddsweb-quantity-controls__subtext); the grid/listing tile (and the same product-tile component rendered outside a grid) uses the BEM buybox classes (online-components-product-tile-buybox-increment/decrement-button__button, count in ...-buybox-quantity__label). Either way: +/- → quantity_add / quantity_remove — the buttons have no text, so eV is their aria-label, e.g. 'add 1 <product name>' / 'remove 1 <product name> from trolley', which the tag falls back to for icon-only controls; the count → quantity with eV '3', re-rendered by Tesco on each change so a fresh appear carries the new count. The third sg rule is a structural fallback for that product-tile component when it is NOT inside a <li data-testid> (its own wrapper divs carry only hashed classes): the container is the div exactly three levels above the tile heading, named from the heading link. For tiles inside the grid the li rule still wins (rules are tried in array order), so it changes nothing there. The tile's favourites button is icon-only with a title ('Save to a Favourites list'), which the same fallback reports as eV. Basket summary — again two markups, grouped by their own stable attribute (sg basket_summary = the trolley-page mini basket, <div aria-label='Basket Summary'>; sg guide_price_grid = the site-header basket, <a data-testid='Guide Price Grid'>) and typed identically so the events line up across both: basket_total = the amount (appear/disappear with eV '£286.54'; Tesco re-renders the summary on basket changes, so each change yields a fresh appear with the new total — if a page ever updates the text in place instead, the total is still carried by the next click's context), basket_link = the whole summary anchor (eV its full text, e.g. '£286.54 Total (estimated)'), basket_button = the header's icon button (eV 'Basket' via aria-label; the icon is a <button> inside the <a>, so a click on the icon attributes to the button, a click on the text to the link), checkout_link = the mini basket's Checkout link — which also gives the study target a precise hook: targetAction event_match { eA: 'click', eT: 'checkout_link' }. Variants share one entry via selector lists (a, b, c) to keep the list short. Mini-trolley items (<ul id='MPBasketSummary'> > <li data-auto='mini-trolley-content-item' data-product-id>): a third quantity markup — + / - are data-auto icon-plus / icon-minus (aria-labels 'Increase <product> by one' / 'Decrease … by one', so eV differs in wording from the tile variants but eT is the same quantity_add / quantity_remove), the count is the <h5> inside output[data-auto='trolley-product-quantity'] (quantity; the h5 is targeted rather than the output so the count is emitted once, not as output + heading), plus two item-only elements: remove_item = the X button (eV 'Remove <product> from basket') and line_price = h5[data-testid='calculated-price'] (eV '£38.00', quantity × unit price). The item's sg rule names it from the title h4 (then the title block, then data-product-id); it sits BEFORE the Basket Summary rule in the array so items keep their product name even if the list is nested inside the summary container. The item's own aria-label ('2 TENA … for £38.00') is deliberately not a name source — it embeds quantity and price, which change. The title link and image link are tracked by the heuristics already (eT link; the image link's eV is the image alt, 'Image of <product>', via the tag's accessible-name fallback). Groceries basket page (<section data-testid='splitbasket-GHSBasketSummary' aria-label='Groceries products'> > ul > <li data-testid='product-list-item'>): a fourth item markup, named from the h3 title link (then the image alt). Its +/- buttons are the ddsweb data-auto pair (already covered); the count is an <input type=number data-auto='ddsweb-quantity-controls-input'> (quantity — note an input reports its type, 'number', on appear/click; the count itself surfaces as a form_change event with eV = the typed value when the shopper types one, while +/- set the value programmatically and fire no change event, so after a +/- click the count is known from the button's aria-label and the line total); the remove X is the item's only icon button WITHOUT a data-auto (remove_item; title/aria-label 'remove <product> from trolley'); the line total is the <p> after the 'Total:' label in the div that follows .ddsweb-buybox__container (line_price = '£31.60' — structural, the wrapper classes are hashed); the per-item checkboxes are typed by their name attribute (note_checkbox = pickerNote, substitutions_checkbox = allowSubstitutions, plus the section-level #subs-checkbox; each is rendered twice — full and short label — with the same id, one hidden by CSS, so expect at most one visible instance's events); save_for_later = the link-button whose aria-label starts 'Save for later'. Elements outside an item (the subs toggle, 'More info', 'Book a slot') group under the section's aria-label, sg groceries_products. The section's primary CTA <a data-testid='checkout-button-GHSBasketSummary'> ('Book a slot', the first step of the groceries checkout) is typed checkout_link alongside the mini basket's Checkout link, so one targetAction covers both routes. Promotional placements — one three-level model for every carousel / panel of stamps, roundels or banners (settled with the client 21 Oct 2026). Every placement is a <div class='ui-panel'> (the CMS layout cell; un-hashed class, often a hashed second class) holding one of four item markups: DDS content stamps (<a class='ddsweb-content-stamp__container'>), DDS icon stamps / roundels (<a class='ddsweb-icon-stamps__container'>), plain roundel links (<a data-testid='roundel-wrapper-<name>'>, promotions page only, Oct 2026) or a DDS banner (<section class='ddsweb-banner__container'>). Level 1 — the PANEL is force-tracked (appear/disappear, eV = the panel's full innerText, 100–600 chars) with a type that says what KIND of placement it is: category_offers = department roundel strips — the untitled strip under the homepage nav (data-testid='roundel-ghs-carousel' with no /brand/ links; 16 roundels 'Groceries & Essentials' … 'Garden, DIY & Car Care'; sg roundel_carousel from the carousel's aria-label) and the promotions page's 'Shop offers by category' strip (data-testid='roundel-special-offers-carousel', 17 links 'All Offers', 'Groceries & Essentials', …; sg shop_offers_by_category); promotions = everything else, including a zone's category-chip navigation — the Christmas zone's 'Navigation Carousel' (data-testid='category-chip-content-carousel', 9 items × 2 stamps 'Tesco Finest Christmas', 'Christmas Gifts', …) together with its grid twin <div data-testid='content-stamp-wrapper'> (16 chips, 'Show more' on narrow screens); sg christmas from the zone h1 inside the panel (typed nav_promotions / nav_promotion until 21 Oct 2026, when the client dropped the nav distinction: the chips are promotion items like any other stamp): the homepage stamp groups ([data-testid='scrollable-content-group'], untitled, sg from the lead stamp headline: sweet__sweet_savings, save_on_selected_finest_cheeses, 20__off_sharkninja, the_ultimate_pro_iphone, …), the promotions page's titled stamp panels (best_deals_from_marketplace_and_f_f, top_savings_on_groceries) and its 'Explore F&F Clothing offers' roundels, 'Shop by brand' roundels (shop_by_brand — a brand placement is a promotion, not a category), zone highlight-group / advanced-content-group stamp grids (New ranges: new_rolled___loaded_buns, …), the zone hero banner (step_into_christmas_2026) and the Christmas zone's brand roundel carousel ([data-testid='content-carousel-wrapper'], untitled → coca_cola from its first label). Level 2 — each ITEM is force-tracked as category_offer / promotion with eV = the item's own text. SG OF AN ITEM (changed 21 Oct 2026 at the client's request): a promotion item carries ITS OWN name as sg — the stamp headline (sweet__sweet_savings, stacks_of_fright_night_bites, 25__off_kids__and_baby_clothing for the three stamps of one homepage group), the roundel label (red_bull, whiskas), the banner headline — NOT the panel's. The first version gave every item its panel's sg, which for an untitled homepage group is the LEAD stamp's headline, so all three stamps of a group reported the first stamp's name (the bug the client saw in the data). The item ↔ panel join is therefore eT + page (the panel's appear precedes its items), not sg. category_offer and (then still) nav_promotion items were aligned the same day (the client saw category_offer 'Marketplace' under shop_offers_by_category while the label span inside it was under marketplace): a category_offer carries its own label (pets, marketplace, all_offers), a Christmas nav chip its chip name (tesco_finest_christmas) — every item type is self-named, only the panel carries the panel name. eV examples: 'Pets', 'Halloween', 'All Offers', 'Red Bull', 'Tesco Finest Christmas', hero stamps 'Sweet, sweet savings\\n\\nTreat yourself …\\n\\nShop deals', the banner 'Step into Christmas 2026\\n\\nThe most wonderful …'. Level 3 — the CONTENT inside an item (image, label span, headline, the stamp anchor itself) has NO config entries: the heuristics track it and the item-level sg rules (content stamp, banner, icon stamp, roundel link) give it sg = the ITEM's name — 'image for Pets' → sg pets, the label click → eT a, eV 'Pets', sg pets — so content ↔ item join directly on sg (same value) for every item type. Why the selectors look the way they do: resolveSemanticGroupFromRules uses element.closest(rule.container) in array order, which is ancestor-OR-SELF, so a force-tracked element always takes the sg of the first rule matching itself or an ancestor. So for an item to carry its OWN name, the force-tracked element must be the item rule's container itself: promotion = the stamp anchor .ddsweb-content-stamp__container on every placement (homepage / promotions-page groups, zone highlight-group / advanced-content-group grids, the Christmas nav chips in both their carousel and grid markup); the icon-stamp anchor .ddsweb-icon-stamps__container (homepage 'Shop by brand' roundels, the promotions page's 'Explore F&F Clothing offers' roundels, the Christmas brand carousel), excluding the department roundel strip [data-testid='roundel-ghs-carousel'] without /brand/ links whose roundels are category_offer — a second selector re-includes the brand variant of that same carousel component; and the banner .ddsweb-banner__container:has(.ddsweb-banner__headline). closest() then matches the item rule on the element itself, the panel rule never gets a turn, and everything inside (img, headline, label span) resolves to the same name. The earlier wrapper-based promotion entries (.ddsweb-grid__column / .ddsweb-carousel__item-container holding a stamp, [data-testid='roundel-wrapper'] around brand roundels, <div class='heroBanner'>) were removed on 21 Oct 2026 — a wrapper sits OUTSIDE the item's container, so closest() fell through to the panel rule and the item took the panel's sg, which was the bug. category_offer follows the same pattern: category_offer = the icon-stamp anchor inside the department strip (.ui-panel without /brand/ links > [data-testid='roundel-ghs-carousel'] .ddsweb-icon-stamps__container; its <div data-testid='roundel-wrapper'> is no longer typed) and the promotions-page roundel link a[data-testid^='roundel-wrapper-'] itself (its .ddsweb-carousel__item-container is no longer typed); the Christmas nav chips are plain .ddsweb-content-stamp__container anchors caught by the promotion entry (the plain <div> around each carousel stamp is no longer typed; the former nav_promotion entry and the promotion entry's exclusions for [data-testid='category-chip-content-carousel'] / [data-testid='content-stamp-wrapper'] went with the rename). Nothing in the config types a wrapper any more; the only way an item could inherit a panel's sg again is a new placement whose item markup matches none of the item sg rules. Harness note: with every item self-named, the CONTAINERS PER RULE 'forced-sg-mismatch' column for the panel rule and the per-panel '(sg!=…)' flags are EXPECTED for every promotion item (the harness compares forced elements with their enclosing container); the checks that matter are 0 heuristic sg, 0 orphans, 0 drift and every img / a inside a stamp showing the stamp's own sg. The Christmas nav carousel is NESTED inside content-stamp-wrapper; with only anchors typed, each chip matches the one promotion entry and is typed once. Panel sg rule: container .ui-panel:has(content stamp, icon stamp, .ddsweb-banner__headline, [data-testid^='roundel-']); name sources in order: (1) 'h2.ddsweb-heading, h1.ddsweb-heading' — 'Shop by brand', 'Shop offers by category', 'Best deals from Marketplace and F&F', the zone h1 'Christmas', the banner h2 'Step into Christmas 2026' (the homepage stamp groups' carousel copy has an EMPTY h2.ddsweb-carousel__title, which querySelector returns first and the tag skips as empty); (2) [aria-roledescription='carousel'] aria-label — the untitled department strip → roundel_carousel; a zone nav carousel without h1 → navigation_carousel; the stamp groups' carousel copy carries only aria-labelledby, so it is skipped; (3) the lead stamp headline (untitled homepage groups: the panel shares its lead stamp's name, eT tells the levels apart); (4) .ddsweb-banner__headline (older h3 banner markup); (5) the first .ddsweb-link__text (untitled roundel carousels → coca_cola). Item sg rules: content stamp = headline → label → aria-label (three markups seen live: offer stamps whose aria-label is the label plus a full stop, trade stamps with no aria-label, hero stamps whose aria-label is the whole 'Headline. Body. CTA.' sentence); banner = headline → aria-label, restricted to banners WITH a headline (:has(.ddsweb-banner__headline)) — the New ranges zone opens with a decorative banner (aria-label literally 'undefined', no headline, no links, empty alt) that is deliberately left unnamed and untyped, its image emits heuristically; icon stamp = label → aria-label → alt; promotions-page roundel link = label span (.ddsweb-link__text > span) → img alt — its <img> is aria-hidden, so a click on the circle walks up to the anchor: eT a, eV 'All Offers', sg all_offers. eV reminders (eV cannot be overridden from config): roundel images 'image for Pets'; nav-chip images and labels equal the chip name; hero-stamp images have an empty or 'null' alt → eV 'image' / 'null', the readable name is the sg; carousel arrows are icon-only → eV is the aria-label. Carousel arrows: carousel_next / carousel_prev on every typed panel (panels holding stamps, icon stamps or a roundel-* carousel; product carousels keep eT button), sg = the panel's (roundel_carousel, shop_by_brand, shop_offers_by_category, christmas, …). Each DDS carousel renders a side pair (desktop) and a bottom pair (mobile), the other pair display:none; the backward arrow is disabled until the carousel has moved (a disabled button fires no click). Desktop / mobile twins: homepage and promotions-page stamp groups render a .ddsweb-grid__column grid (visible desktop) AND a .ddsweb-carousel__item-container carousel (visible mobile) of the SAME stamps (homepage: 56 stamp anchors in the desktop DOM, 46 in the mobile DOM, each typed promotion with its own name; the hidden copy emits nothing); the Christmas nav renders the chip grid (desktop, 16) and the Navigation Carousel (mobile, 16). The harness flags each as rendered-on-one-breakpoint; they are counterparts, both typed, same sg and eID in both viewports. Verified 21 Oct 2026 with the tag injected and this config, desktop (1400×1000, desktop UA, mouse clicks) and mobile (412×915, Android UA, touch taps), on the homepage, /groceries/en-GB/promotions, /shop/en-GB/category/christmas and /shop/en-GB/zone/new-ranges: 0 heuristic sg, 0 orphans, 0 sg drift between viewports (31 / 33 / 28 / 24 common containers); homepage: category_offers (sg roundel_carousel) with 16 category_offer items, 8 promotions panels with their promotion items, every roundel image / label click and tap → eT img / a with the roundel's sg, stamp image click → eT img with the stamp's sg, arrows → carousel_next / carousel_prev with the panel sg (desktop side pair, mobile bottom pair); promotions page: category_offers (shop_offers_by_category) with 17 category_offer items, circle and label clicks → eT a with the link's sg, next and back arrows → carousel_next / carousel_prev; Christmas zone: the nav panel (then nav_promotions, sg christmas) with 16 items per viewport (then nav_promotion (mobile carousel items sg christmas, desktop grid items self-named), chip label tap → eT a sg tesco_finest_christmas, brand roundels → promotion (panel coca_cola; items self-named since the change below), hero banner → promotions + promotion under step_into_christmas_2026; New ranges: 8 promotions panels, 17 self-typed promotion stamps, headline click → eT promotion; two independent loads per viewport of the homepage and the promotions page gave identical sg / eT / eID / forced types for all 40 / 37 containers. Re-verified 21 Oct 2026 after promotion items became self-named, desktop (1400×1000, mouse) and mobile (412×915, Android UA, touch), on the homepage, /groceries/en-GB/promotions, /shop/en-GB/category/christmas and /shop/en-GB/zone/new-ranges: 56 / 46, 16 / 16, 38 / 38, 17 / 17 stamp anchors typed promotion with their own headline as sg, 0 heuristic sg, 0 orphans, 0 sg drift (31 / 33 / 28 / 24 common containers); stamp image click and tap → eT img with that stamp's sg (sweet__sweet_savings, stacks_of_fright_night_bites, 25__off_kids__and_baby_clothing for the three stamps of one group), headline click and tap → eT promotion with the same sg, brand / clothing roundel label → eT promotion sg red_bull / coca_cola / women, hero banner → promotion sg step_into_christmas_2026 (its h2 stays eT h2 — already tracked, never re-attributed); department roundels unchanged (16 category_offer under roundel_carousel, labels eT a); two independent homepage loads identical per viewport (41 / 40 containers, 0 changed signatures). The homepage 'Get the most out of Tesco' link panel renders on desktop only (10 vs 9 promotions panels), a site layout choice, not a hook gap. Re-verified again 21 Oct 2026 after category_offer and the nav chips became self-named too, desktop and mobile, on the homepage, /groceries/en-GB/promotions, /shop/en-GB/promotions (the URL the client's event came from; same page) and the Christmas zone: homepage 16 / 16 department roundels typed category_offer with their own label as sg (groceries___essentials, special_offers, halloween), label click and tap → eT category_offer, circle click and tap → eT img 'image for Groceries & Essentials', both with the roundel's sg; promotions page 17 / 17 roundel links typed category_offer (all_offers, groceries___essentials, marketplace), label and circle click and tap → eT category_offer with the link's sg (the img is aria-hidden, the anchor takes the click); Christmas zone 16 carousel chips (mobile) and 16 grid chips (desktop) typed with the chip name as sg (tesco_finest_christmas, christmas_gifts, advent_calendars), label click and tap → the chip's own name as sg (eT nav_promotion at the time,