ge eT img, prices, value bar, badge, add button, all with the product's sg; the join is tile ↔ content on sg). Three tile markups, one entry each, chosen so the typed element is exactly what the matching sg rule names: (1) grid tile <li data-testid='<id>'> (search / browse; 29 on the whisky search); (2) carousel tile <section data-testid='product-<id>' data-product-id> (homepage rails, 117; promotions page, ~280); (3) the structural fallback for the product-tile component rendered inside a plain DDS carousel (search-page 'Marketplace' and sponsored rails, 56 on the whisky search): div:has(> div > div > h2.online-components-product-tile-product-heading__heading), excluding li[data-testid] * and section[data-product-id] * so a tile is typed once. One of those rails wraps the tile in an extra <div>, so the first attempt — typing .ddsweb-carousel__item-container — missed 24 of 85 tiles and would have put the forced element OUTSIDE its sg container (heuristic sg); typing the sg rule's own container fixes both. Star rating: <div data-testid='star-rating' class='ddsweb-rating__container'> = five SVG stars (the first carries aria-label 'Average customer rating 4.8 out of 5 stars', role img) + <p class='ddsweb-rating__hint' aria-hidden>4.8 (92)</p>; typed rating, eV = the hint text '4.8 (92)' = grade and (review count) in one value — there is no separate review-count element on a tile, and the SVG cannot be typed on its own (an SVG has no innerText, the tag would emit 'text'). One markup on every page seen (search, promotions, zone rails). Not every product has a rating (whisky search: 27 of 29 grid tiles; homepage rails: none) — a tile without stars simply emits no rating event. A click/tap on the stars attributes to the rating element (eT rating, eV '4.7 (275)', the product's sg). Verified 21 Oct 2026, desktop (1400×1000, mouse) and mobile (412×915, touch): whisky search — 85 / 85 tiles typed product in both viewports (29 li + 56 structural), rating 51 / 51, 0 heuristic sg, 0 orphans, 0 sg drift over 13 common containers, rating clicks and taps in the grid and in the rails → eT rating, title click/tap → eT a, image → eT img, all with the tile's sg; two independent loads differ only in the sponsored slots (different products in the same positions, same eID and typed set per position), the other 23 containers identical; promotions page — 278 / 284 section tiles typed product (lazy carousels render a few more on the phone), rating 124 / 131, 0 drift over 33 containers, rating / image / title clicks and taps → rating / img / a; homepage — 117 / 117 section tiles typed product, no star ratings rendered there. The product detail page could not be dumped (Tesco's Akamai check blocks the headless browser on /shop/en-GB/products/… and /groceries/en-GB/products/…), so the PDP's rating / review-count markup is unverified — add a selector once seen. Clubcard value bar (both tile variants, Oct 2026 build): <a class='ddsweb-value-bar__container' href='/promotions/<id>'> — the whole bar is a LINK to the offer page and carries no data-testid any more (the earlier [data-testid='value-bar'] hook is gone, so the previous price_promo / promo_terms entries matched nothing). Entries are class-based now: price_promo = '£4.00 Clubcard Price', price_promo_unit = '(£8.00/litre)', promo_terms = 'Offer valid for delivery from … until …', price_promo_link = the bar anchor itself (a click anywhere on the bar attributes to it; eV is the bar's full text). Carousel tiles on the promotions page (<section data-testid='product-<id>' data-product-id aria-label='<name>'>) now render the SAME product-tile component as the grid (online-components-product-tile-price__text / unit-price__subtext / buybox-add-button), so the carousel sg rule still groups them and the grid price entries carry the prices; the .ddsweb-price__container / .tile-delivery-message / data-auto quantity entries were seen only on a marketplace sample and are kept as inert fallbacks. Re-render check (Oct 2026, headless Chrome with the tag injected and this config): two independent homepage loads, a scroll pass, a hero-carousel rotation and a search-grid re-render (sort/count change, pushState URL) all produced identical sg and eID for every stamp, banner and tile, and every forced element inside a tile resolved to its tile's sg. Viewport check (20 Oct 2026, homepage + search 'milk', desktop 1400x1000 with mouse clicks AND mobile 412x915 Android UA with touch taps, same config): Tesco serves the same DOM at both breakpoints for everything above — identical match counts for every selector (113 carousel tiles / 46 stamps on home, 25 grid tiles / 11 value bars on search), identical sg per container, zero heuristic sg, zero orphans, and taps on the tile image / price attribute to the same eT (img, price_retail) as mouse clicks (promotional placements: see the three-level section above); the sort re-render is signature-identical on mobile too. The one breakpoint-specific component is the basket entry: on mobile the mini basket ([aria-label='Basket Summary'] with basket_total / basket_link a[data-auto='basket-icon'] / checkout_link a[data-auto='mini-trolley-checkout']) is present in the DOM but display:none, so those entries emit nothing on a phone; for a guest with an empty basket the mobile search page shows no basket control at all (the only '#mfe-basket' anchor is a hidden 'Skip to basket' accessibility link, deliberately not tracked). The mobile basket path (header icon / sticky bar once items are added, trolley page) is NOT yet verified — it needs a logged-in or non-empty session; until then the basket_* / checkout_link entries are desktop-verified only and mobile basket events should not be expected in the data. Hover events are desktop-only by nature (no sustained hover on touch). Not covered: any grid-tile promotion slot not seen in the sample — if Clubcard prices there render as a ddsweb value bar they are already caught by the value-bar entries; otherwise add a selector once seen. With the sg rules active each of these events carries its product's name as sg and the entry's type as eT. Homepage marketplace offer carousel (added 21 Oct 2026 from a client sample; a fourth product-tile markup): a lazily rendered DDS carousel (<div class='ddsweb-carousel__content-mask'> > #ddsweb-ghs-carousel-_r_15_ > <div class='ddsweb-carousel__item-container' data-key aria-label='item N' role='group'>) whose items are a NEW, lighter product-tile component — a hashed wrapper div holding the image link (a.online-components-product-tile-product-link__link > img with an EMPTY alt), an <h3 class='online-components-product-tile-product-heading__heading'> whose link text is the product name (the other tile variants use an h2), an 'Offer' <span class='ddsweb-tag__container'> and the price <p data-testid='price-text'>; no data-product-id, no aria-label, no buybox. Per the client only the ITEMS matter, not the carousel: each tile is force-tracked as product_offer (appear/disappear, eV = the tile's innerText 'Ezysleep Deluxe … Air Bed\\n\\nOffer\\n\\n£49.99') with sg = the product name, and the carousel / its panel is deliberately untyped (its arrows stay eT button, since the carousel_next / carousel_prev entries are scoped to stamp and roundel panels). The sg container and the typed element are the same node — the tile div identified structurally as div:has(> h3.online-components-product-tile-product-heading__heading) (the wrapper's own classes are CSS-module hashes), so closest() resolves on the element itself and nothing inside falls through to a heuristic sg; it is disjoint from the h2-based rules and entries, so the earlier product typing is untouched (0 matches for the new selector on the live homepage, promotions page, new-ranges zone and marketplace home in both viewports). Name sources: the h3 link text, then the h3 itself. Inside a tile: the image click/tap → eT img, eV 'image' (empty alt; the readable name is the sg), the title click/tap → 